## 2. Foundations and Problem Definition
Hu, Lu, and Clune name the problem of automating such design ADAS [ [18](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B18-preprints-216468)], extrapolating from features and architectures to agents themselves. ADAS targets the automatic design of precisely that complete object.

## 7. Search over Modular Agents and Architectures
### 7.1. From Open-Ended Code Search to Structured Architecture Search
The earliest formulation of ADAS treats an agent as an arbitrary program and lets a meta agent write new agents from scratch, collecting discoveries in an archive [ [18](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B18-preprints-216468)].

**AgentSquare** is the analogue of cell-based NAS, but on the agent side [ [42](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B42-preprints-216468)].

## 8. Evolutionary and Self-Evolving Agents
An increasingly prominent branch of ADAS conceives of building agents as open-ended iteration: agents, or the meta-systems that produce them, are gradually transformed by mutation, recombination, and selection. It draws on quality-diversity / open-endedness (MAP-Elites [ [31](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B31-preprints-216468)]) and recursive self-improvement (Schmidhuber’s Gödel machine [ [41](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B41-preprints-216468)]).

### 8.2. Symbolic Learning and Recursive Self-Modification
Gödel Agent [ [55](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B55-preprints-216468)] “leverages LLMs to dynamically modify its own logic and behavior, guided solely by high-level objectives through prompting” [ [55](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B55-preprints-216468)] via introspection and runtime monkey-patching; unlike ADAS [ [18](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B18-preprints-216468)], it “recursively updates both the policy π and the meta-learning algorithm I” [ [55](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B55-preprints-216468)], sacrificing provable optimality for noisy hill-climbing in which a single bad rewrite can corrupt the agent.

## 13. Challenges, Limitations, Safety, and Directions for Future Work
ADAS has matured exceptionally fast—from Meta Agent Search, which programs new agents as code [ [18](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B18-preprints-216468)], to recursively self-improving systems such as Gödel Agent [ [55](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B55-preprints-216468)] and the Darwin Gödel Machine (DGM) [ [62](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202606.0238#B62-preprints-216468)]—and in doing so has outpaced our understanding of when these systems work, how much they cost, and whether they are safe.

